{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed change of use from the rear of commercial unit (Use Class E) to residential unit (Use Class C3) would result in the loss of floorspace for a commercial unit which sits within a neighbourhood centre, and the development fails to demonstrate a need for this facility in this location, the development is deemed to be unacceptable and contrary to:·&nbsp;Paragraph 93 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023)Policy E9 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DME3 and DME5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development would present&nbsp;one small low-quality balcony due to its siting abutting the highway and proximity to the external flues of the commercial units, thus displaying a poor quality of external amenity space.&nbsp;Furthermore, the proposed bike storage and refuse and recycling storage would be located internally within the open plan kitchen/living space with no separation to the main dwelling, thus taking up internal floor space, reducing the GIA of the house and risking harmful odours spreading through the habitable space, creating a sub-standard quality of accommodation., contrary to:DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Policy D6 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD 1 and Part 6 of policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)London Cycling Design Standards (September 2016)Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)",
    "The proposed development by reason of its scale, bulk, height, represents poor design, failing to respect the architectural design of the surrounding area, lacks articulation and interest and would not fit in with the character of the area, contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023)Policies D1 and D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
